import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Robot Kit with Bluetooth Control" description="Open source, Bluetooth-controlled wheeled robot kit for learning robotics basics, built around the ScoutMakes Azul board.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Kit · Open Source Hardware</p>
  <h1>ScoutMakes Robot Kit with Bluetooth Control</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Robotics and industrial automation are everywhere — this kit teaches the basics by building a small,
    wheeled robot you can drive from your phone.
  </p>

  <p>
    Everything needed to assemble a fun little robot friend is included. Thanks to the included ScoutMakes Azul
    board, you send drive instructions over BLE from an app on your iOS or Android device — simply tilt your
    device in the direction of travel.
  </p>

  <ul class="spec-list">
    <li>Quick, solder-and-snap assembly (assembly guide and all mechanical hardware included)</li>
    <li>Controllable over BLE using an iOS or Android app</li>
    <li>Piezoelectric buzzer for sound feedback</li>
    <li>Powered by a rechargeable LiPo battery (105&nbsp;mAh)</li>
    <li>Four NeoPixels (RGB) for illumination</li>
    <li>Modifiable, 3D-printable chassis source files</li>
    <li>Quality N20 motors with metal gearboxes and rubber tires</li>
    <li>DRV8833 dual H-bridge motor driver</li>
    <li>Powered by an ARM Cortex M4F (with hardware floating point) at 64&nbsp;MHz</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    <a href="/learn/robot-kit-assembly">Assembly instructions</a> and design files, including the Tinkercad
    chassis source project, are provided for building and hacking the kit.
  </p>

  <div class="buy-panel">
    <h2>Where to buy</h2>
    <p>Sold through our distributor network — pricing and stock vary by region.</p>
    <div class="buy-links">
